WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.556 --> 00:00:03.036
Mihawk took Zoro in because of Luffy.

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:08.546
Have you ever be so bored that you went out
of your way to start beef with a Yonko?

00:00:08.546 --> 00:00:10.586
Well, me neither.

00:00:10.586 --> 00:00:12.656
However, this guy has.

00:00:12.656 --> 00:00:17.495
Mihawk is an incredibly interesting character
in the story for a number of reasons.

00:00:17.495 --> 00:00:21.175
As the strongest swordsman, his strength and
position in the hierarchy of the One Piece

00:00:21.175 --> 00:00:25.976
world, are probably one of the most heatedly
discussed topics in the fandom at this point.

00:00:25.976 --> 00:00:29.876
And while there are probably just as many
people who find this debate pointless as those

00:00:29.876 --> 00:00:36.996
who blow it way out of proportion, Mihwak's
power actually is a big part of his character.

00:00:36.996 --> 00:00:41.096
Because even though he might not seem like
the type, being one of the most stoic and

00:00:41.096 --> 00:00:46.926
serious characters in the story, Mihawk has
a surprisingly interesting character arc,

00:00:46.926 --> 00:00:52.046
starting all the way back at the Baratie and
coming to a close with him taking Zoro in

00:00:52.046 --> 00:00:57.676
as his student.

00:00:57.676 --> 00:01:02.475
And so, even though Mihawk rarely actively
appears in the story, he actually plays a

00:01:02.475 --> 00:01:08.276
really important role for the One Piece world
building overall, but especially so for Zoro

00:01:08.276 --> 00:01:11.926
and his journey towards becoming the strongest
swordsman in the world.

00:01:11.926 --> 00:01:16.825
So, how did Mihawk change as a character during
and after Marineford?

00:01:16.825 --> 00:01:18.926
How strong is he really?

00:01:18.926 --> 00:01:20.776
What's the deal with him and Perona?

00:01:20.776 --> 00:01:24.435
And will he fight Zoro and Shanks again in
the future?

00:01:24.435 --> 00:01:30.076
This is the story of the strongest swordsman,
rival to Shanks and former warlord of the

00:01:30.076 --> 00:01:31.076
sea.

00:01:31.076 --> 00:01:39.795
This is the story Dracule Mihawk.

00:01:39.795 --> 00:01:50.785
At his introduction early on in the story,
Mihawk serves as a

00:01:50.785 --> 00:01:55.736
Sign-post of how strong people in the world
of One Piece truly are.

00:01:55.736 --> 00:01:59.865
As a fellow warlord, he brilliantly sets the
stakes for the Baroque works saga and the

00:01:59.865 --> 00:02:01.356
fight against Crocodile.

00:02:01.356 --> 00:02:05.946
I already talked a lot about all the symbolism
that is associated with Mihawk in my Scene

00:02:05.946 --> 00:02:09.936
analysis of his fight with Zoro in Baratie,
so if you are interested in that, I suggest

00:02:09.936 --> 00:02:12.195
you check that video out afterwards.

00:02:12.195 --> 00:02:18.566
To sum it up, like most swordsmen in the story,
Mihawk has a very strong religious theme going,

00:02:18.566 --> 00:02:21.826
giving him the appearance of a Spanish inquisitor.

00:02:21.826 --> 00:02:25.646
This mostly serves to show the duality of
both his strong dedication to his beliefs

00:02:25.646 --> 00:02:30.396
and creed, while at the same time highlighting
his violent, unforgiving and strict side as

00:02:30.396 --> 00:02:40.356
well, just as the Catholic church used to
be, during The Inquisition.

00:02:40.356 --> 00:02:46.986
This creed that Mihawk follows, is not Christianity
however, but the Bushido, the path of the

00:02:46.986 --> 00:02:52.146
samurai, that Zoro also follows, although
approached through a Buddhist lens, while

00:02:52.146 --> 00:02:56.746
shanks represents nordic mythology and its
values and beliefs.

00:02:56.746 --> 00:03:03.106
Long story short, swordsmanship, and by that
I mean REAL swordsmanship is a sort of religion

00:03:03.106 --> 00:03:04.846
in the world of One Piece.

00:03:04.846 --> 00:03:17.236
And only true believers and followers can
rise in the ranks of the very best.

00:03:17.236 --> 00:03:22.415
This serves as the framework for the interactions
and relationships Mihawk has with Zoro and

00:03:22.415 --> 00:03:23.415
Shanks.

00:03:23.415 --> 00:03:27.516
All have quite different beliefs, values and
powers, but they all respect the Bushido,

00:03:27.516 --> 00:03:32.626
and thus are worthy opponents, when it comes
to sword fighting that is.

00:03:32.626 --> 00:03:35.456
This is regardless of their actual power level.

00:03:35.456 --> 00:03:40.217
The reason why Mihawk suddenly started respecting
Zoro and treating him as a worthy opponent

00:03:40.217 --> 00:03:45.596
is not because Zoro suddenly became as strong
as him, but because he demonstrated his will

00:03:45.596 --> 00:03:58.546
to follow the path of the swordsman to 
the death, and Major spoiler from the manga,

00:03:58.546 --> 00:04:04.496
please skip ahead 10 seconds if you aren't
caught up, of course by that will, I also

00:04:04.496 --> 00:04:08.776
mean Zoro's conqueror’s haki that Mihawk
most likely saw when he used the three thousand

00:04:08.776 --> 00:04:09.865
worlds against him.

00:04:09.865 --> 00:04:15.836
We have this short moment, as Zoro launches
his attack where Mihawk is clearly shocked

00:04:15.836 --> 00:04:20.826
by this reveal, as it serves as the ultimate
proof of Zoro’s will and potential to make

00:04:20.826 --> 00:04:22.676
it to the top.

00:04:22.676 --> 00:04:27.976
So how is it that Mihawk went from seeing
Zoro as a potential future rival, to becoming

00:04:27.976 --> 00:04:30.786
his mentor throughout the time skip?

00:04:30.786 --> 00:04:35.236
Let's look at Mihawk's surprisingly deep character
arc.

00:04:35.236 --> 00:04:38.356
Writing a great character arc is actually
pretty damn hard.

00:04:38.356 --> 00:04:41.986
And as with all new skills you want to learn
things, it helps having someone explain it

00:04:41.986 --> 00:04:43.496
to you in great detail.

00:04:43.496 --> 00:04:47.266
And that is exactly what Skillshare is all
about.

00:04:47.266 --> 00:04:51.886
Skillshare is an online learning community
with thousands of inspiring classes for creative

00:04:51.886 --> 00:04:56.386
and curious people covering pretty much any
topic you might ever want to learn about.

00:04:56.386 --> 00:05:00.716
Be it starting a YouTube channel or how to
make your very own Manga.

00:05:00.716 --> 00:05:05.516
I've been using Skillshare for quite sometime,
mostly to improve my work here on YouTube.

00:05:05.516 --> 00:05:06.516
For example, if you write yourself, I recommend
this excellent course on character arcs.

00:05:06.516 --> 00:05:08.386
But It can really be anything.

00:05:08.386 --> 00:05:13.116
For example I personally have really enjoyed
this course on knife skills by Elana Karp

00:05:13.116 --> 00:05:18.556
recently, so I can slice my Onions in true
Mihawk fashion now.

00:05:18.556 --> 00:05:21.986
And look, there is even a class on Bladesmithing.

00:05:21.986 --> 00:05:25.656
If you also love learning new skills, then
you should definitely give Skillshare a try.

00:05:25.656 --> 00:05:30.106
Not only is it pretty affordable, with under
10 bucks per month for an annual subscription,

00:05:30.106 --> 00:05:34.656
but the first 1000 people to use my link in
the description will get a free trial of Skillshare

00:05:34.656 --> 00:05:37.486
Premium so you can try it for yourself.

00:05:37.486 --> 00:05:50.256
But, now back to my fellow knife master.

00:05:50.256 --> 00:05:54.966
Mihawk's perspective on the central moral
theme of One Piece, freedom, is that the best

00:05:54.966 --> 00:06:01.746
thing is to be a lone wolf, bound by no-one
and seeking out other wolves to test his strength.

00:06:01.746 --> 00:06:06.416
Or I guess in his case it's actually a lone
hawk.

00:06:06.416 --> 00:06:11.216
One might even say he’s a me-hawk.

00:06:11.216 --> 00:06:14.846
The major turning point for Mihawk was the
war at Marineford.

00:06:14.846 --> 00:06:18.886
Before the war, we get introduced to him as
an extremely self-centered person.

00:06:18.886 --> 00:06:23.416
He is pretty much the only strong person out
there operating completely without a crew

00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:25.756
or any other people around to support him.

00:06:25.756 --> 00:06:31.506
He is literally a one-man crew, that sails
the seas bored out of his mind as he has no-one

00:06:31.506 --> 00:06:40.876
to test his ridiculous strength on.

00:06:40.876 --> 00:06:44.876
This becomes especially clear in his relationship
with Shanks.

00:06:44.876 --> 00:06:51.316
Regardless of Haki, Shanks was powerful enough
as a swordsman alone to spar evenly with Mihawk,

00:06:51.316 --> 00:06:53.896
leading to the legendary rivalry between them.

00:06:53.896 --> 00:06:58.156
No doubt Mihawk came looking for Shanks quite
often to have a duel.

00:06:58.156 --> 00:07:04.146
But when Shanks sacrifices his arm for Luffy
and inspiring him to become a pirate, Mihawk

00:07:04.146 --> 00:07:09.996
doesn't care at all about his motivations
and the reasons, he simply sees Shanks sacrificing

00:07:09.996 --> 00:07:15.336
his strong sword arm as an insult to their
rivalry and doesn't even bother to draw his

00:07:15.336 --> 00:07:20.016
sword against him.

00:07:20.016 --> 00:07:28.986
Shanks, the only man who was able to excite
Mihawk, gave up on being a top tier swordsman

00:07:28.986 --> 00:07:31.206
for a mere kid.

00:07:31.206 --> 00:07:35.896
Given that Shanks has ridiculous haki abilities,
he probably doesn't care about that though,

00:07:35.896 --> 00:07:42.196
and their rivalry turned into a sort of friendship.

00:07:42.196 --> 00:07:52.976
However, that left Mihawk with absolutely
no-one to rival with and test his skills on

00:07:52.976 --> 00:07:57.466
and he ended up so bored and aimless, that
he chased after powerful people like Don Krieg,

00:07:57.466 --> 00:08:08.066
just to get a bit of a kick.

00:08:08.066 --> 00:08:13.286
This self-centered person, who only cared
about strength, would not have accepted Zoro’s

00:08:13.286 --> 00:08:17.336
show of throwing away his pride as a Swordsman
by bowing to him.

00:08:17.336 --> 00:08:20.876
This is basically what Shanks did in Mihawk’s
eyes.

00:08:20.876 --> 00:08:28.086
And so it's no surprise that this proud, ridiculously
powerful swordsman, despite becoming a warlord,

00:08:28.086 --> 00:08:31.866
was never really willing to follow the directions
of the world government.

00:08:31.866 --> 00:08:35.976
What made the war at Marineford different,
was not the fact that he was scared of the

00:08:35.976 --> 00:08:41.076
government’s repercussions, as we just saw,
Mihawk didn't really care at all about losing

00:08:41.076 --> 00:08:46.216
his warlord title, no, the reason he participated
in this war, was because he would be able

00:08:46.216 --> 00:08:54.876
to challenge Whitebeard.

00:08:54.876 --> 00:08:58.886
The strongest man in the world vs the strongest
swordsman.

00:08:58.886 --> 00:09:04.756
Basically Mihawk went to Marineford for a
kick – to fight the only man he believed

00:09:04.756 --> 00:09:06.286
worth fighting.

00:09:06.286 --> 00:09:10.986
And yet, when he showed his hand, Jozu, shielded
his captain from his attack.

00:09:10.986 --> 00:09:15.406
It begins to dawn on Mihawk that Whitebeard
wasn't only feared because of the beast of

00:09:15.406 --> 00:09:22.326
a person he was, but also because of all the
people he had gathered around him.

00:09:22.326 --> 00:09:26.896
And later, the very same thing happens again
with Luffy.

00:09:26.896 --> 00:09:31.016
Deciding to test his resolve and power again,
after already having taken an interest in

00:09:31.016 --> 00:09:36.526
him at Baratie, more and more of Luffy’s
allies kept getting in Mihawk’s way.

00:09:36.526 --> 00:09:42.276
At this point, Mihawk understands that the
ability of gathering allies is the greatest

00:09:42.276 --> 00:09:52.206
power he’s seen on the seas.

00:09:52.206 --> 00:09:56.516
And yet, his mind doesn't change here yet
completely.

00:09:56.516 --> 00:10:01.016
When Shanks arrives to end the war, he realizes
that there are no more worthy opponents left

00:10:01.016 --> 00:10:05.456
to fight and he leaves, Shanks is the last
person he wants to fight after he ruined their

00:10:05.456 --> 00:10:11.196
rivalry, and of course to be fair also because
Shanks as a yonko is most likely just out

00:10:11.196 --> 00:10:14.336
of his league when he uses his haki.

00:10:14.336 --> 00:10:19.836
Things really only change for Mihawk after
the war, as Zoro is transported to his island.

00:10:19.836 --> 00:10:25.646
And it is this interaction between them, that
brings Luffy's impact on Mihawk to full bloom.

00:10:25.646 --> 00:10:31.176
Zoro is the only character, as far as we know,
who Mihawk hopes can grow to one day challenge

00:10:31.176 --> 00:10:32.176
him.

00:10:32.176 --> 00:10:36.896
And yet Zoro is telling him that fighting
for the self-centered greatest Swordsman pride,

00:10:36.896 --> 00:10:48.896
something that Mihawk only cares about, does
is no longer his motivation.

00:10:48.896 --> 00:10:54.096
Zoro wants to become the strongest swordsman
in order to help Luffy become pirate king.

00:10:54.096 --> 00:10:57.876
At first this leaves Mihawk disgusted.

00:10:57.876 --> 00:11:02.426
He thinks that Zoro is weak and wasn't even
strong enough to beat the monkeys on the island,

00:11:02.426 --> 00:11:06.186
that were trying to imitate him, by the way
a really nice metaphor for what he thinks

00:11:06.186 --> 00:11:11.326
of most other swordsmen, and he believed that
Zoro came asking him for help to get off the

00:11:11.326 --> 00:11:12.346
island.

00:11:12.346 --> 00:11:17.236
And yet for the very first time, these things
are now becoming personal to Mihawk with added

00:11:17.236 --> 00:11:18.486
perspective.

00:11:18.486 --> 00:11:22.926
When he sees that Zoro had beaten all the
monkeys and could leave whenever he wanted

00:11:22.926 --> 00:11:28.606
to, Mihawk realizes that Zoro is asking for
help for Luffy's sake and not his own which

00:11:28.606 --> 00:11:37.346
is why he agrees to train him.

00:11:37.346 --> 00:11:41.866
Mihawk finally listens to Zoro and accepts
his plea given that he’s seen that fighting

00:11:41.866 --> 00:11:46.566
for others is worthwhile in its own right
since Luffy and Whitebeard fought for Ace

00:11:46.566 --> 00:11:51.686
and in turn very many people fought for them
as well, ultimately making his presence at

00:11:51.686 --> 00:11:57.856
the war irrelevant, as he was never willing
to go all out anyways.

00:11:57.856 --> 00:12:02.676
Mihawk is no longer the lone wolf, realizing
that having someone by your side to fight

00:12:02.676 --> 00:12:05.946
for, is what gives one true freedom and purpose.

00:12:05.946 --> 00:12:10.846
And so, the fact that he lets Perona and Zoro
stay with him on his island for two years,

00:12:10.846 --> 00:12:16.416
forming real relationships for the first time,
is something prewar Mihawk would never have

00:12:16.416 --> 00:12:17.416
been able to do.

00:12:17.416 --> 00:12:22.436
And I ultimately believe that Mihawk’s character
arc would be fully completed if he ever decided

